  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Error purging object demo:998, underlying Exception:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Caused by: java.io.IOException: Failed to delete file: ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "D:\\Fedora34\\fedora\\data\\datastreamStore\\61\\info%3Afedora%2Fdemo%3A998%2FDS1%2FDS1.0",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at org.akubraproject.fs.FSBlob.delete(FSBlob.java:129) [akubra-fs-0.3.jar:na]",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at org.akubraproject.impl.BlobWrapper.delete(BlobWrapper.java:117) [akubra-core-0.3.jar:na]",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.akubra.AkubraLowlevelStorage.delete(AkubraLowlevelStorage.java:456) ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "On closer inspection, this is due to an InputStream not being closed in:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "org.fcrepo.server.storage.translation.AtomDOSerializer.setManagedContent(Entry entry, Datastream vds), line 418:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "IOUtils.copy(vds.getContentStream(), m_zout);",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Replacing with the following resolves the issue:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "InputStream is = vds.getContentStream();",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "IOUtils.copy(is, m_zout);",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "is.close();",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "From ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://commons.apache.org/io/api-release/org/apache/commons/io/IOUtils.html:"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://commons.apache.org/io/api-release/org/apache/commons/io/IOUtils.html:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "\"Wherever possible, the methods in this class do not flush or close the stream. This is to avoid making non-portable assumptions about the streams' origin and further use. Thus the caller is still responsible for closing streams after use. \"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Given this, might be worth a bit of a general code trawl-through for other instances of IOUtils to ensure streams are closed correctly where they should be.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "(I'm pretty sure I have used IOUtils.copy() without thinking about closing streams afterwards.  And this might explain why I end up with so many temp files that are not deleted).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Curious as to why this was not an issue with the legacy low-level storage implementation.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
