  "description": "<p>Error purging object demo:998, underlying Exception:</p>\n\n<p>Caused by: java.io.IOException: Failed to delete file: </p>\n\n<p>D:\\Fedora34\\fedora\\data\\datastreamStore\\61\\info%3Afedora%2Fdemo%3A998%2FDS1%2FDS1.0<br/>\n\tat org.akubraproject.fs.FSBlob.delete(FSBlob.java:129) <span class=\"error\">&#91;akubra-fs-0.3.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n\tat org.akubraproject.impl.BlobWrapper.delete(BlobWrapper.java:117) <span class=\"error\">&#91;akubra-core-0.3.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n\tat org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.akubra.AkubraLowlevelStorage.delete(AkubraLowlevelStorage.java:456) </p>\n\n<p>On closer inspection, this is due to an InputStream not being closed in:<br/>\norg.fcrepo.server.storage.translation.AtomDOSerializer.setManagedContent(Entry entry, Datastream vds), line 418:</p>\n\n<p>                    IOUtils.copy(vds.getContentStream(), m_zout);</p>\n\n<p>Replacing with the following resolves the issue:</p>\n\n<p>                    InputStream is = vds.getContentStream();<br/>\n                    IOUtils.copy(is, m_zout);<br/>\n                    is.close();</p>\n\n<p>From <a href=\"http://commons.apache.org/io/api-release/org/apache/commons/io/IOUtils.html:\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://commons.apache.org/io/api-release/org/apache/commons/io/IOUtils.html:</a></p>\n\n<p>\"Wherever possible, the methods in this class do not flush or close the stream. This is to avoid making non-portable assumptions about the streams' origin and further use. Thus the caller is still responsible for closing streams after use. \"</p>\n\n<p>Given this, might be worth a bit of a general code trawl-through for other instances of IOUtils to ensure streams are closed correctly where they should be.</p>\n\n<p>(I'm pretty sure I have used IOUtils.copy() without thinking about closing streams afterwards.  And this might explain why I end up with so many temp files that are not deleted).</p>\n\n<p>Curious as to why this was not an issue with the legacy low-level storage implementation.</p>",
